'.agent_tasks/four-lenses-cli-textual_mixins/README.md', 'content': "# Four 
Lenses Bug Report: src/henchman/cli/textual_mixins.py\n## Date: 
2025-03-17T06:00:00Z\n## Bug Summary\nThe `_textual_confirm` method has a race 
condition where if the confirmation screen callback is invoked after the future 
has already been cancelled (due to an exception or app shutdown), it will 
attempt to call `future.set_result()` on a cancelled future, which raises 
`asyncio.InvalidStateError`.\n\n## Lens\n**Phase 2: State & Side Effects (The 
Entropy Audit)** - Shared state synchronization issue between exception handlers
and callback functions.\n\n## Expected vs. Observed\n| Expected Behavior | 
Observed Risk |\n|---|---|\n| Callback should safely handle already-cancelled 
futures | Callback may raise `asyncio.InvalidStateError` when trying to set 
result on cancelled future |\n| Exception handlers and callbacks should 
coordinate cleanup | Race condition between exception cleanup and callback 
invocation |\n| Futures should be in valid state when operations are performed |
Futures can be cancelled while callback is still pending |\n\n## Root Cause\nThe
`_callback` function inside `_textual_confirm` checks `if not future.done():` 
before calling `future.set_result()`, but a future can be in the `CANCELLED` 
state without being `done()`. In asyncio, `cancelled()` is a separate state from
`done()`. When `future.cancel()` is called in the exception handlers, the future
transitions to cancelled state but `future.done()` may still return `False` 
initially. The callback then tries to `set_result()` on a cancelled future, 
which raises `asyncio.InvalidStateError`.\n\n## Fix Plan\nModify the callback to
check `if not future.done() and not future.cancelled():` before calling 
`set_result()`. This ensures we don't try to set a result on a cancelled future.
Also add proper synchronization to ensure callback and exception handlers don't 
interfere.\n\n## Status: IN PROGRESS"})

